I thought non-wielding monks could still throw stuff, which they'd
want enchanted as highly as possible. +2 (or more) blessed ammo lasts
longer, and +7 daggers hurt a lot more. I'll let the people who have
ascended such characters decide that part. You also have to find and
ID enchant weapon before you go around using a pickaxe.

Also notice that I specified a blessed scroll, which might mean using
some holy water.

Third, this conduct has two points:
a) The player can do less damage, as they get no artifact weapon. This
is the challenge part.
b) The player has to be careful with their keystrokes. This is
arguably either a challenge or a nuisance imposed by the interface.

Using the above idea does not make the challenge in part (a) any
easier, but does make part (b) not so annoying.

Compared to other conducts, (think genoless, wishless, etc.)
weaponless is the only one with such high proportion of part (b).
Object-polyless has a small part in that you have to be carful when
dipping, self-polyless requires you to be careful to search for
polytraps, or wear magic resistance. I don't think the carefulness
part should be removed completely, but the idea above would help a
player who wanted the challenge and was willing to go out of their way
to suppress the annoying part.

